From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 23:58:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] UefiPayloadPkg/FmpDeviceSmmLib: Write only the regions of a
 manifest that fits

The library writes the regions named by the manifest of an image; with
no manifest, or when the regions are not where the image puts them in
the flash, or the FMAP of the flash can't be read, it writes the whole
BIOS region of the image, or the whole flash. That also replaces what a
manifest leaves alone: the variable store, with the settings, boot
entries and Secure Boot keys, and regions written once per machine, like
the vital product data with its serial number, which an image built for
every machine has empty. And a whole-flash write stops at the first
region the descriptor protects from the host, with the flash half
written.

Refuse such images instead, from the image check on, and drop the
fallbacks and the descriptor parsing they used. A firmware whose flash
layout changes is installed with an external tool, which can carry
those regions over. Report why in the last attempt status of the ESRT,
with the codes of this library: the image, the layout, or the writing.

Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
